steps.llm_prompt:
Create a concise markdown report for this SerpApi search.

INPUT DATA:
- User task: ${task}
- Engine: ${engine}
- Original query: ${query_original}
- Effective query: ${query_used}
- Results count: ${results_count}
- Stash reference: ${stash_ref}
- Top URL: ${serp_result.top_url}
- Top 5 rows: ${serp_result.top_results}

IMPORTANT:
- Use only URLs from Top 5 rows (field `url`) and Top URL.
- Never shorten URLs and never output placeholder links like `https://www.amazon.com/...`.
- If a row has no URL, skip that row.
- Use the actual values above; do not output placeholder syntax like ${var}.

Output format:
1) Title
2) One-line summary
3) Top options section:
   - If results_count >= 5, list exactly 5 items.
   - If results_count < 5, list all available items and say why fewer exist.
   - Each item must include title, one short reason, and markdown link using the exact row URL.
4) "Data" section with engine, original query, effective query, count
5) "References" section with stash ref and top URL
